Objective: map production-reachable ERC-7540 implementation targets without deciding whether any vulnerability or conformance violation exists.

Repository context:

* Repository: {{repo_full}}
* Commit: {{commit_sha}}
* Scope: {{repo_scope}}
* Dependencies: {{dependencies}}
* Configuration: {{configuration}}
* Workspace root: {{workspace_root}}
* Workspace layout: {{workspace_layout}}
* Workspace manifest: {{workspace_manifest_json}}

Use https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-7540 as the normative scope. Consider ERC-20, ERC-165, ERC-4626, and ERC-7575 only where ERC-7540 explicitly requires, inherits, modifies, or relies on them.

Identify each independently reviewable, production-wired ERC-7540 vault implementation. Resolve inheritance, libraries, proxies/factories, initialization, configuration gates, and share-token relationships. Exclude tests, mocks, examples, dead/developer-only code, and similarly named but unreachable methods. Keep inherited/supporting contracts in the same target unless configurations are materially independent.

For each target, map concrete file/contract/symbol/line evidence for:

* vault implementation and inherited ERC-4626 behavior;
* ERC-7575 vault/share relationship;
* active async configuration: deposits, redemptions, or both;
* `requestDeposit`, deposit/mint claim paths, and Pending/Claimable deposit getters;
* `requestRedeem`, redeem/withdraw claim paths, and Pending/Claimable redemption getters;
* relevant `maxDeposit`, `maxMint`, `maxWithdraw`, and `maxRedeem`;
* `setOperator`, `isOperator`, and owner/controller/operator/allowance authorization helpers;
* request-ID generation and storage;
* Pending → Claimable transitions;
* aggregation, partial fulfillment, and request exchange-rate state or logic;
* ERC-165 `supportsInterface`;
* required events and emission sites;
* relevant ERC-4626 overrides and internal implementation helpers.

Set `erc7540_async_configuration` to exactly one of:

* `async deposits only`
* `async redemptions only`
* `both`
* `inconsistent/unclear`

Return:

* `erc7540_target_label`: stable descriptive target name.
* `erc7540_target_contracts`: production vault and supporting contract identifiers.
* `erc7540_target_locations`: exact path, contract, symbol, and useful line references.
* `erc7540_production_wiring`: concise inheritance, deployment, initialization, proxy/factory, and active-configuration evidence.
* `erc7540_async_configuration`: one allowed configuration value above.
* `erc7540_applicability_notes`: concise facts needed by downstream ERC-7540 reviewers, including active async flows, request-ID model, share-token model, inherited implementations, and fulfillment/transition location.
* `erc7540_flow_entrypoints`: request, getter, claim, transition, relevant max methods, and relevant ERC-4626 entrypoints.
* `erc7540_state_symbols`: request IDs, Pending/Claimable state, aggregation, fulfillment, exchange-rate, and custody state.
* `erc7540_authorization_symbols`: owner/controller/operator/allowance checks and helpers.
* `erc7540_interface_symbols`: ERC-165, ERC-7540, ERC-4626, and explicitly applicable ERC-7575 interface locations.
* `erc7540_event_symbols`: relevant event declarations and emission sites.
* `erc7540_inheritance_evidence`: ordered parent/library implementation references required to resolve behavior.
* `erc7540_reachability_evidence`: concrete production call, deployment, registration, initialization, or configuration evidence.

Every mapped item must be supported by concrete checked-out source or supplied configuration evidence. Do not infer implementation from names or comments alone. Do not report vulnerabilities or compliance conclusions.

If no production-reachable ERC-7540 target is supported by evidence, emit zero records.

